# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# studio/.env — template. Copy to `studio/.env` and fill in. `.env` is
# gitignored at any depth, so studio/.env is already covered.
#
# This file is committed and must NEVER hold a real value.
#
# The Sanity token belongs HERE and not at the repo root:
# migration-scripts/sanity/import.mjs calls loadEnv('studio'), so it reads
# studio/.env. The Webflow token is the opposite case — pull.mjs calls
# loadEnv() and reads the root .env. Putting either in the other file fails
# with a missing-variable exit that names the file it expected.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Sanity auth token. Read by migration-scripts/sanity/import.mjs
# (`npm run sanity:import`) and by nothing else.
#
# Where: sanity.io/manage -> the project -> API -> Tokens -> Add API token.
# Scope: WRITE (Editor or above). The import creates documents and uploads the
#        images the converter emitted as `_sanityAsset: "image@<url>"`, so a
#        read-only token fails partway through rather than up front.
#
# This is the only step in the whole migration that needs network AND a write
# token. Convert stays offline; §2, §3 and §5 need no token at all.
SANITY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT A SECRET, AND NORMALLY ABSENT.
#
# The Studio's dataset override. The real value is project.jsonc's
# sanity.dataset. `guard-production-deploy.mjs --studio` checks the root and
# studio env files plus the shell for this, and blocks `npm run studio:deploy`
# if it is set to anything other than production.
#
# Consume with `||`, never `??` — an unfilled key here loads as ''.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET=
